# Zetra Blue End User Licence Agreement (EULA)

DRAFT. Fill in the remaining [SQUARE BRACKETS] before you publish this, and have a lawyer check it. It is not legal advice.

## 1. The licence
Aober Aura Studio ("we") gives you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence to install and use Zetra Blue and the Zetra colour tabs and tools that come with it ("the software") for your own projects, under this EULA, the Terms of Service and the Policies. We keep all rights we do not give you here. The software is licensed, not sold.

## 2. Who gets this licence for free
You may use the software free of charge if you are an individual, a hobbyist, a student, a small creator, or a small team that is not a Large Organization. You may sell what you make with it.

## 3. Large Organizations
A "Large Organization" is any company, group or body that, together with the companies it controls or is controlled by, had more than [1,000,000] in yearly revenue or funding, or has more than [10] people working for it, in its last financial year. A Large Organization does not get this licence. It needs a separate written agreement with us before it installs, uses, hosts, resells, builds on or embeds the software. A person may not use the software on behalf of a Large Organization, including as a contractor, without that agreement. Splitting a company into pieces to stay under the threshold does not count.

## 4. What you may do
- Use the software on your own devices to make your own work.
- Keep copies for backup.
- Change the plain scripts for your own use, if they are provided as source. Your changes are still covered by this EULA.
- **Ship what the software makes.** Games, templates, shaders, exports and the small runtime files the tools copy into your project (for example VNPlayer, DynamicBone, VTuberTracker, AntiCraft and the game templates) may be distributed inside your own projects, free of charge, including in commercial projects. Keep any copyright and licence notices that come with those files, for example in your credits or a licence file. Do not distribute them on their own, in a pack, or as an asset or tool for others to build with (see section 5). A Large Organization needs the written agreement in section 3 first.

## 5. What you may not do
- Sell, rent, lend, sub-license, host or share the software or any part of it on its own, or put it in a pack, asset store or service, without our written permission. (Section 4 covers what you ship inside your own projects.)
- Scrape, crawl or bulk-copy the software, its documents or its data, by hand or by machine, from any device, including an iPhone.
- Reverse engineer, decompile or take apart anything not provided as plain source, or copy its way of working through a clean-room or "clean engineering" process.
- Use it, its outputs or its documents to build, train or test a competing product.
- Remove or hide our name, notices or this EULA.
- Use it to make content the Policies forbid.
- Share a template pack or other file made to harm people's computers or data.
This applies as far as the law allows. A right the law gives you and that cannot be waived stays yours.

## 6. Your content
You keep ownership of everything you make. We do not claim it, collect it or train anything on it. You promise that you have the right to use everything you put into the software, and that you follow the Policies, including the rules for adult content.

## 7. Files you convert or import
Zetra Blue can read and convert files from other programs (for example .unitypackage, .fbx, .psd, .kra, .docx, shaders and avatars). You may only convert or import files you have the right to use. Converting a file does not give you any rights to it and does not change the licence it came with (for example a store licence, an avatar licence or a paid shader licence). Those licences still apply to the result.

## 8. Third-party parts and services
Parts made by others stay under their own licences (see THIRD_PARTY.md). Nothing in this EULA changes those licences. Some tools can start other programs you installed yourself (such as ffmpeg, Blender, Python or tpm2-tools) or contact services you choose to use (such as the Claude API with your own key in AntiCraft Chat). Those programs and services are not ours. Their terms, prices and privacy rules apply, and you are responsible for your own accounts and keys with them.

## 9. Not affiliated
Zetra is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Microsoft, Google, Adobe, Unity, VRChat, Poiyomi, the Blender Foundation, the Krita project, OpenSeeFace, Anthropic, Valve or any other company or product named in the software or its documents. Their names are used only to say which formats or ideas a tool relates to. All trademarks belong to their owners.

## 10. Updates and ending
We may update or stop the software at any time. This licence ends if you break it. When it ends, stop using the software and delete your copies. What you made with it stays yours.

## 11. No warranty and limits
The software is provided "as is". The science, maths and engineering tools (Zetra Purple) are for learning and quick checks, not for safety-critical, medical or professional use. As far as the law allows we are not liable for lost data, lost income or indirect damage. Nothing here limits liability that the law does not allow us to limit.

